---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
  <!-- Subtle grid background -->
  <div class="grid-bg"></div>

  <!-- Navigation -->
  <nav class="nav">
    <div class="nav-inner">
      <a href="/" class="brand">Nan Shang</a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a href="#systems">Systems</a>
        <a href="#research">Research</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <h1 class="h1">
          I build systems<br/>
          that last.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Chief Scientist & Founding Engineer at Drone Institute.
          <br/>Designing geospatial and AI systems that remain stable,
          <br/>correct, and maintainable under real operational pressure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Divider -->
  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <main class="container">

    <!-- Overview -->
    <section class="section">
      <p class="body-large">
        My work sits at the intersection of remote sensing research, geospatial analytics,
        and system architecture. I focus on building systems that take spatial data—often
        noisy, incomplete, and operationally constrained—and turn it into outputs that can
        be trusted in real decision-making contexts.
      </p>
      <p class="body-large">
        What matters is not isolated model performance, but how a system behaves end to end:
        how data enters, how assumptions propagate, how errors surface, and how the system
        evolves under continuous use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Principles -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="h2">Principles</h2>
      
      <div class="principles">
        <div class="principle">
          <h3 class="h3">Production is the benchmark</h3>
          <p class="body">
            A system is only meaningful if it continues to behave correctly after deployment.
            I design systems to fail visibly rather than silently, to support iteration without
            destabilization, and to remain interpretable to engineers and operators.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle">
          <h3 class="h3">Constraints shape architecture</h3>
          <p class="body">
            Latency, throughput, cost envelopes, and operational friction are architectural facts.
            I treat these constraints as inputs to design decisions, making trade-offs explicit
            so systems can be reasoned about and maintained over time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle">
          <h3 class="h3">Deployment reveals assumptions</h3>
          <p class="body">
            Research does not end at deployment. I design feedback loops that surface failure modes,
            quantify drift, and allow systems to improve without eroding trust or stability.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principle">
          <h3 class="h3">Data quality compounds</h3>
          <p class="body">
            Long-term system advantage comes from disciplined data practices. I build pipelines
            where ingestion, annotation, quality control, monitoring, retraining, and rollback
            strategies reinforce one another.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Systems -->
    <section class="section" id="systems">
      <h2 class="h2">Systems</h2>

      <div class="systems">
        <div class="system">
          <div class="system-meta">
            <span class="system-type">Pipeline</span>
            <span class="system-status">Active</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h3">End-to-End Geospatial Pipelines</h3>
          <p class="body">
            Full lifecycle—ingestion, normalization, processing, verification, reporting, delivery.
            Designed to be repeatable, auditable, and resilient under scale.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="system">
          <div class="system-meta">
            <span class="system-type">Sensing</span>
            <span class="system-status">Active</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h3">Multimodal Remote Sensing Workflows</h3>
          <p class="body">
            RGB imagery, thermal and infrared data, derived spatial layers. Extracting actionable
            signals while controlling uncertainty and false positives in operational environments.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="system">
          <div class="system-meta">
            <span class="system-type">Quality</span>
            <span class="system-status">Active</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h3">Verification & Quality Control Systems</h3>
          <p class="body">
            Automated and human-in-the-loop verification layers that make spatial failures—projection
            errors, alignment drift, metadata assumptions—observable and traceable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="system">
          <div class="system-meta">
            <span class="system-type">Delivery</span>
            <span class="system-status">Active</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h3">Secure Data Delivery Architectures</h3>
          <p class="body">
            Multi-tenant access control, lifecycle management, permission boundaries, and audit-friendly
            access patterns with strict tenant isolation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Research -->
    <section class="section" id="research">
      <h2 class="h2">Research</h2>
      <p class="body-large">
        My research background is in remote sensing and geospatial analysis, and it directly
        informs the systems I build today. My peer-reviewed work addresses questions that recur
        in production systems:
      </p>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>How spatial measurements behave under noise and scale</li>
        <li>How resolution, alignment, and representation affect downstream inference</li>
        <li>How to reason about uncertainty in derived spatial products</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="body">
        I have authored and co-authored publications in journals and conferences, contributing
        methods and analytical frameworks that are now embedded in production pipelines.
      </p>
      <div class="link-row">
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en" 
           target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link">Google Scholar →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact -->
    <section class="section" id="contact">
      <h2 class="h2">Contact</h2>
      <div class="contact">
        <div class="contact-item">
          <span class="contact-label">Primary</span>
          <a href="mailto:nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai" class="contact-link">
            nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-item">
          <span class="contact-label">Personal</span>
          <a href="mailto:sn1514826@gmail.com" class="contact-link">
            sn1514826@gmail.com
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-item">
          <span class="contact-label">GitHub</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/leibowivz" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="contact-link">
            github.com/leibowivz
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="footer-content">
        <div>
          <div class="footer-name">Nan Shang, Ph.D.</div>
          <div class="footer-role">Chief Scientist & Founding Engineer, Drone Institute</div>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/leibowivz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en" 
             target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scholar</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <style>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PROFESSIONAL MINIMALIST DESIGN
       Inspired by: Apple, Linear, Stripe leadership pages
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    :root {
      --black: #000000;
      --gray-900: #0a0a0a;
      --gray-800: #1a1a1a;
      --gray-700: #2a2a2a;
      --gray-500: #737373;
      --gray-400: #a3a3a3;
      --gray-300: #d4d4d4;
      --white: #ffffff;
      
      --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
      --border-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
      
      --font-sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --font-mono: "SF Mono", "Monaco", "Inconsolata", "Fira Code", monospace;
      
      --ease: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
    }

    body {
      background: var(--black);
      color: var(--white);
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      line-height: 1.6;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
    }

    /* ═══ GRID BACKGROUND ═══ */
    .grid-bg {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      background-image: 
        linear-gradient(var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px),
        linear-gradient(90deg, var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px);
      background-size: 100px 100px;
      opacity: 0.3;
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 0;
    }

    /* ═══ NAVIGATION ═══ */
    .nav {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      z-index: 100;
      background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
      backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .nav-inner {
      max-width: 1200px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 1.5rem 3rem;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .brand {
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--white);
      text-decoration: none;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .nav-links {
      display: flex;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .nav-links a {
      color: var(--gray-400);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      transition: color 0.2s var(--ease);
    }

    .nav-links a:hover {
      color: var(--white);
    }

    /* ═══ CONTAINER ═══ */
    .container {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 10;
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 3rem;
    }

    /* ═══ HERO ═══ */
    .hero {
      min-height: 85vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      padding-top: 6rem;
    }

    .hero-content {
      max-width: 800px;
    }

    .h1 {
      font-size: 4.5rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--gray-400);
      font-weight: 400;
    }

    /* ═══ DIVIDER ═══ */
    .divider {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 10;
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto 8rem;
      height: 1px;
      background: var(--border);
    }

    /* ═══ SECTIONS ═══ */
    .section {
      position: relative;
      margin-bottom: 8rem;
    }

    .h2 {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    .h3 {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .body-large {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: var(--gray-400);
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .body {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--gray-400);
    }

    .list {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 2rem 0;
    }

    .list li {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--gray-400);
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      position: relative;
    }

    .list li::before {
      content: "—";
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      color: var(--gray-500);
    }

    /* ═══ PRINCIPLES ═══ */
    .principles {
      display: grid;
      gap: 3rem;
    }

    .principle {
      padding-bottom: 3rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .principle:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    /* ═══ SYSTEMS ═══ */
    .systems {
      display: grid;
      gap: 3rem;
    }

    .system {
      padding-bottom: 3rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .system:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    .system-meta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .system-type {
      color: var(--gray-500);
    }

    .system-status {
      color: var(--gray-400);
    }

    /* ═══ LINKS ═══ */
    .link-row {
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .link {
      color: var(--white);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 1rem;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      transition: opacity 0.2s var(--ease);
    }

    .link:hover {
      opacity: 0.7;
    }

    /* ═══ CONTACT ═══ */
    .contact {
      display: grid;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .contact-item {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      padding-bottom: 2rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .contact-item:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    .contact-label {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      color: var(--gray-500);
    }

    .contact-link {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      color: var(--white);
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: opacity 0.2s var(--ease);
    }

    .contact-link:hover {
      opacity: 0.7;
    }

    /* ═══ FOOTER ═══ */
    .footer {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 10;
      margin-top: 12rem;
      padding: 4rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .footer-content {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    .footer-name {
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .footer-role {
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      color: var(--gray-400);
    }

    .footer-links {
      display: flex;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .footer-links a {
      color: var(--gray-400);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      transition: color 0.2s var(--ease);
    }

    .footer-links a:hover {
      color: var(--white);
    }

    /* ═══ RESPONSIVE ═══ */
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .container {
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
      }

      .nav-inner {
        padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem;
      }

      .nav-links {
        gap: 1.5rem;
      }

      .h1 {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
      }

      .lead {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
      }

      .h2 {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
      }

      .hero {
        min-height: 70vh;
      }

      .footer-content {
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 2rem;
      }

      .footer-links {
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1rem;
      }
    }

    /* ═══ SUBTLE ANIMATIONS ═══ */
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      a, .link, .contact-link {
        transition: opacity 0.2s var(--ease);
      }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
